8 Practical Steps to Humanize Your Writing (Manually)
1. Carefully review flagged sections  
Start by examining the sentences or paragraphs flagged by AI content detection tools. Look for rigid phrasing, overly symmetrical sentence structures, or generic transitions (this can also appear in genuinely human-written academic text). 

2. Rework text for natural academic flow 
Read the text aloud or revise it line by line. Vary sentence openings and rhythm to improve flow. Small, deliberate stylistic adjustments often reduce false positives more effectively than trying to bypass AI detection using automated tools. 

3. Simplify without flattening the meaning 
AI writing tools can sometimes overexplain or repeat ideas when generating responses. Use your judgement to avoid unnecessary oversimplification and cull out redundancy to achieve clear, concise, nuanced drafts that reflect human authorship. 

4. Vary structure and strengthen transitions 
Ensure ideas progress logically across paragraphs. Use signposting and smoothen transitions to guide readers through your research argument, rather than relying on uniform paragraph sizes or generic connectors commonly seen in AI-generated content. 

5. Restore author voice and disciplinary context 
Academic humanization is not about sounding conversational, it is about making your stance, reasoning, and expertise visible. So add your interpretations, emphasize key points, or include real-world examples from your field to reflect your authentic voice.  

6. Verify all facts, claims, and references  
AI humanizers can sometimes add grammar errors, alter context, or introduce inaccuracies while rewriting. Carefully verify your data, check for missing citations, and clarify claims to ensure accuracy and alignment with your original intent. 

7. Be transparent and document your process 
It is recommended to save drafts, revision notes, and version histories when working with AI. If needed, this record can demonstrate authorship and responsible AI use to support any discussions around AI content detection results. 

8. Stay compliant by disclosing AI use clearly 
Most importantly, follow your institutional or journal AI guidelines to ensure transparency and build credibility. Guidelines do allow for responsible AI use as long as the author(s) are accountable and take full ownership of their work. Including clear AI disclosures with your submissions can protect academic integrity and allay doubts around inappropriate AI usage. 